        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ian Hunter, Rob Thomas\n- Bands: Mott the Hoople, Matchbox 20\n- Albums: Dirty Laundry, ...Something to Be\n- Songs: Streetcorner Symphony\n\nFacts:\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939 and is known professionally as Ian Hunter.\n- Rob Thomas was born on February 14, 1972 as Robert Kelly Thomas.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from the band's inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974.\n- Ian Hunter was also the lead singer of Mott the Hoople during the band's 2009 and 2013 reunions.\n- Rob Thomas is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist best known as the lead singer of Matchbox 20.\n- Dirty Laundry is the eighth solo album by Ian Hunter.\n- Streetcorner Symphony is the fifth and final single from Rob Thomas's solo album ...Something to Be.",
